<title>BOTSWANA: Barclays yr shr trebled, div doubled.</title>
<headline>Barclays yr shr trebled, div doubled.</headline>
<dateline>GABORONE 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>		    (million pula unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (thebe)			 121.22   vs   38.97</p>
<p>    Final div (thebe)  35.0 making 60.00   vs   30.00</p>
<p>    Net income			  136.04   vs   108.38</p>
<p>    Net interest income		83.39   vs   68.88</p>
<p>    Other operating income	   52.56   vs   39.50</p>
<p>    Bad/doubtful debt charge	  1.07   vs   11.40</p>
<p>    Pre-tax				51.91   vs   18.59</p>
<p>    Tax				    10.59   vs   5.31</p>
<p>Full name: Barclays Bank of Botswana Ltd</p>
<p>Div payable May 29</p>
<p>On register May 16</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said the strong performance reflected measures taken to control costs and improve profitability over the last two years.</p>
<p>Net interest income had increased by 21 percent in 1996 due to an increase in holdings of Bank of Botswana Certificates, not an increase in lendings. The opportunities for quality lending had remained limited.</p>
<p>-- Gaborone newsroom +267 347182</p>
</text>
